OL,3,GNEWSABrother's shock as cancer claims
OL,4,Asister in 24 days
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Worcestershire man whose sister died
OL,7,Fjust 24 days after being diagnosed with
OL,8,Fblood cancer, has spoken of how he went
OL,9,Ffrom planning her recovery to arranging
OL,10,Fher funeral in less than a month.
OL,12,FJeff Farnes, from Redditch, said
OL,13,Fdoctors initially believed his sister
OL,14,FHelen Bryan's acute myeloid leukaemia
OL,15,F(AML) had been caught early and could
OL,16,Fbe treated.
OL,18,FBut despite an encouraging prognosis
OL,19,Fand weeks of treatment that appeared to
OL,20,Fbe going well, the 57-year-old died
OL,21,Fless than a month after receiving the
OL,22,Fdiagnosis.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
